EOF
}

help_tidy_cargo() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Deletes old cargo artifacts under target/ and keeps the current build. Each unit cargo still
builds keeps its newest output: the debug and release binaries, test harnesses, and each feature
set, such as moqui-core with and without its default features. A later cargo build of unchanged
code does not recompile.

Cargo names a unit's files with a hash of the compiler, the profile, the features, and the
dependency graph. The hash changes when one of those changes, and cargo leaves the previous
files in place. Repeated builds fill target/debug/deps and target/debug/incremental with those
old copies. rustc already drops old incremental sessions inside one of those directories; this
removes the directories for hashes the current build does not use. A build script's run
fingerprint does not record the profile or the features, so each run that a kept library names
stays, along with its output under build/.

It does not remove target/debug/moqui, target/release/moqui, or target/moqui-app. A cargo build
that is running is left alone. load-save does not run this.
EOF
}

help_opensearch_download() {
    cat <<EOF
Downloads opensearch-min for Linux (x64 or arm64) into runtime/opensearch. The version
defaults to $OPENSEARCH_VERSION. An archive already in runtime/ is used instead of downloading.
OpenSearch publishes no macOS tarball; on macOS run it another way and set elasticsearch_url.

Options:
  -f, --force          Replace an existing runtime/opensearch, deleting its data
EOF
}

help_opensearch_start() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Starts runtime/opensearch as a daemon (bin/opensearch -d -p pid). The server uses a node that
answers and only starts its own when nothing does and there is no pid file, so a daemon started
here outlives server restarts.
EOF
}

help_opensearch_stop() {
